		<div id="content" class="container group" rol="main">
			<div class=" col-9">

		<!-- article page -->
		<script>var postdate=new Date('2026-09-11T07:29:43+00:00')</script>
		<article class="h-entry">
				<div class="article individual no-image group">
					<div class="info group">
							<h1 class="title full-article p-name"><a class="u-url" href="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/2026/09/active-matter-developers-put-up-an-incredibly-distasteful-ai-notice-on-steam/">Active Matter developers put up an incredibly distasteful AI notice on Steam</a></h1>
							<div class="subtitle"></div>
							<div class="meta"><time class="dt-published" datetime="2026-09-11T07:29:43Z">11 Sep 2026 at 7:29 am UTC</time>  | Last updated: 11 Sep 2026 at 1:20 pm UTC <strong>[updated]</strong> <br>
								By <strong><a rel="author" href="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/profiles/2/">Liam Squires-Hand</a></strong>
								<span class="hide-small"></span> <div class="comments-pip"><a title="Comments Link" href="#comments">34 comments</a></div>  
							</div>
					</div>
					<div class="content group e-content">
						<p>Active Matter from Gaijin Network Ltd looks like a lot of fun for fans of first-person shooters, but they soured it with a truly distasteful AI notice.</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><img title="Active Matter - Gaijin Network Ltd" src="https://uploads.golmedia.net/uploads/articles/article_media/6005366321789111634gol2.webp" alt="Active Matter - Gaijin Network Ltd" width="1200" height="675"></p>
<p>This isn't even getting into my own personal thoughts on generative AI, but rather the attempt from developer Matter Team to dive into what I assume is supposed to be an edgy joke. The problem is, what they said is just so abhorrent that I am amazed someone actually signed off on having this published to the official Steam page:</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><img title="The developers describe how their game uses AI Generated Content like this:  In-game AI character Ms. Second is using AI generated voice. Using humans voices for AI character would be cultural appropriation." src="https://uploads.golmedia.net/uploads/articles/article_media/1032151351789111234gol2.webp" alt="The developers describe how their game uses AI Generated Content like this:  In-game AI character Ms. Second is using AI generated voice. Using humans voices for AI character would be cultural appropriation." width="944" height="164"></p>
<blockquote>
<p>The developers describe how their game uses AI Generated Content like this:</p>
<p>In-game AI character Ms. Second is using AI generated voice. Using humans voices for AI character would be cultural appropriation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Cultural appropriation. Really? That's what we're going with? I'm pretty lost for words on the stupidity here.</p>
<p>Their PR team did already send over review keys to GamingOnLinux, and I asked them what they were thinking with this notice and to clarify how generative AI is being used (I assume they are actually using AI for that voice) and I am yet to receive a reply. I will update if they do reply.</p>
<hr>
<p><strong>Update - 10:39 UTC</strong> - Gaijin replied and simply said:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>"We do not use generative AI for anything other than for Ms. Second. And even there, the choice is deliberate: we use an AI-generated voice not to cut costs, or speed up production, but because we see it as a postmodern artistic statement – an AI character quite literally speaking with an AI-generated voice"</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Update #2 - 13:04 UTC</strong> - Gaijin followed up to say:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>"In other words, we think AI should be voiced by AI - not to offend AI. This feels especially important nowadays, with AGI almost here. That's all we can say, unpacking the whole AI cultural narrative isn’t really our place."</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That…just…I'm completely lost for words. Pure stupidity. I'm baffled by their thinking. Either they've <em>completely</em> lost the plot on AI or they're determined to go deep into what they see as a joke without thinking about the industry at all, and how stupidly insensitive it is to joke about cultural appropriation.</p>
<div class="itemdb_embed"><div class="info_header"><span class="info_title"><a href="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/itemdb/app/48885/active-matter/">Active Matter</a></span></div><div class="info_grid"><div class="info_row steam_rating_row"><span class="label">Steam Deck</span> <span class="value"><a href="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/guides/view/what-steam-deck-steam-machine-steam-frame-and-steamos-verified-ratings-mean/">🟡 Playable</a></span></div><div class="info_row"><span class="label">Platform:</span> <span class="value"><a href="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/guides/view/how-to-check-game-compatibility-for-linux-steamos-and-steam-deck/">&#128039; Native Linux</a></span></div><div class="info_row"><span class="label">Release Date:</span> <span class="value">📅 15th September 2026</span></div><div class="info_row"><span class="label">Devs:</span><span class="value"><a href="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/itemdb/developer/655">Gaijin Network Ltd</a>, <a href="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/itemdb/developer/3570">Matter Team</a></span></div><div class="info_row"><span class="label">Official links:</span><span class="value store-links"><a class="btn-store" href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/2887580/Active_Matter/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Steam</a></span></div></div></div>
						
