								<div class="actual-comment-text" id="text_299898">
									<blockquote class="comment_quote"><cite>Quoting: <span class="username">Nezchan</span></cite><blockquote class="comment_quote"><cite>Quoting: <span class="username">ShabbyX</span></cite>It looks sarcastic to me, taking a jab at people who call other ridiculous stuff as cultural appropriations. No? 🤔<br>
<br>
I can&#039;t imagine them being serious in such a claim.<br>
</blockquote>Much more likely, it&#039;s the type who spends a lot of their time complaining about &quot;the woke&quot; and thinks it&#039;s clever or edgy to use the language of their culture war opponents without taking even a second to understand what they mean.<br>
</blockquote>You&#039;re talking about the same thought process viewed from a different angle.<br>
You would consider x amount of time spent complaining about &quot;the woke&quot; a lot and ShabbyX would consider a complaint of x amount of silliness too silly to be taken seriously.<br>
<br>
I would like to request you to not get in a slugfest about, which perspective should be taken, since both conclude that they&#039;re ridiculing people they dislike.<br>
Yet, I also admit the right to endlessly dispute about, which of these perspectives is best is your right under Article 19 of the universal declaration of human rights, so feel free to fight about it if you need it.
								</div>
