						<a class="anchor" id="r299927"></a>
						<div class="comment group r299927 ">
							<div class="comment-meta group">
								<div class="comment-post">
									<span class="username"><img title="Manjaro" class="distro tooltip-top" alt="" src="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/templates/default/images/distros/Manjaro.svg"><a href="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/profiles/18009">Johnologue</a></span>  <abbr title="2026-09-12T11:50:49+00:00" class="timeago">12 Sep 2026</abbr>  
								</div>
								<div class="comment-actions">
									<ul>
										<li><a class="tooltip-top" href="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/index.php?module=articles_full&amp;go=report_comment&amp;article_id=29744&amp;comment_id=299927" title="Report"><span class="icon flag">Flag</span></a></li>
										   
										<li><a href="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/2026/09/active-matter-developers-put-up-an-incredibly-distasteful-ai-notice-on-steam/?comment_id=299927" data-ajax-modal data-page="comment" data-id="299927" data-type="comment" class="post_link tooltip-top" title="Link to this comment"><span class="icon link">Link</span></a></li>
										
									</ul>
								</div>
							</div>
							<div class="comment-author hide-xsmall">
								<div class="avatar"><img class="avatar" src="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/uploads/avatars/generated/18009_generated_1783590474.png" alt="User Avatar"></div>
								<ul class="comment-badges">
									
									
									
								</ul>
								<ul class="comment-social">
									
								</ul>
							</div>
							<div id="299927" class="comment-body">
								<div class="actual-comment-text" id="text_299927">
									I feel like the offhand joke about &quot;cultural appropriation&quot; from robots isn&#039;t necessarily even edgy or belittling the <em>concept</em> of cultural appropriation. I&#039;m sure I&#039;ve seen very socially conscious left-leaning folks make similar jokes without malice.<br>
<br>
<blockquote class="comment_quote">&quot;In other words, we think AI should be voiced by AI - not to offend AI. This feels especially important nowadays, with AGI almost here. That&#039;s all we can say, unpacking the whole AI cultural narrative isn’t really our place.&quot;</blockquote>Like, I think this <em>is</em> pretty ridiculous. AGI isn&#039;t &quot;almost here&quot;, and AI isn&#039;t going to be offended at AI not being used. They probably should have said the last sentence <em>&quot;we&#039;re not going to add fuel to the fire here, it&#039;s not our job to talk out the AI cultural narrative&quot;</em> without first adding fuel to the fire.<br>
<br>
I just don&#039;t think the original joke is bad. It might have read worse because of a perceived association between edgy right-wing people and pro-AI views; I&#039;ve been called &quot;woke&quot; for a &quot;no AI was used&quot; notice, so I see the connection...but the AI disclaimer is <em>just</em> for the voice...so they&#039;re hardly NFT-bro maximalists. They would&#039;ve used it WAY more.<br>
<br>
I will also acknowledge, human voice actors can play robot characters very well! GLaDOS was voiced by a person imitating a speech synthesizer, and that definitely made the character much more powerful and memorable. I won&#039;t complain a robot voice is being used for a robot, but I also will say, there&#039;s another way that&#039;s pretty cool, too.
								</div>
							<div class="likes"><span class="total_likes">3</span> Likes <span class="who-likes"><span class="emoji-summary"><span style="margin-right: 5px;">👍 (3)</span></span> <a href="#" data-ajax-modal data-page="likes" data-type="comment" data-id="299927">See more...</a></span></div>
							</div>
						</div>

						
						<a class="anchor" id="r299941"></a>
						<div class="comment group r299941 ">
							<div class="comment-meta group">
								<div class="comment-post">
									<span class="username"><img title="CachyOS" class="distro tooltip-top" alt="" src="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/templates/default/images/distros/CachyOS.svg"><a href="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/profiles/573">scaine</a></span>  <abbr title="2026-09-12T17:49:48+00:00" class="timeago">12 Sep 2026</abbr>  
								</div>
								<div class="comment-actions">
									<ul>
										<li><a class="tooltip-top" href="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/index.php?module=articles_full&amp;go=report_comment&amp;article_id=29744&amp;comment_id=299941" title="Report"><span class="icon flag">Flag</span></a></li>
										   
										<li><a href="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/2026/09/active-matter-developers-put-up-an-incredibly-distasteful-ai-notice-on-steam/?comment_id=299941" data-ajax-modal data-page="comment" data-id="299941" data-type="comment" class="post_link tooltip-top" title="Link to this comment"><span class="icon link">Link</span></a></li>
										
									</ul>
								</div>
							</div>
							<div class="comment-author hide-xsmall">
								<div class="avatar"><img class="avatar" src="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/uploads/avatars/scaine328_avatar.png" alt="User Avatar"></div>
								<ul class="comment-badges">
									<li><span class="badge pale-green">Contributing Editor</span></li> <li><span class="badge light-purple">Mega Supporter</span></li>
									<li><a href="#" data-ajax-modal data-page="computer_deets" data-id="573">View PC info</a></li>
									
								</ul>
								<ul class="comment-social">
									<li><a href="http://scaine.net" title="External Link: http://scaine.net"><span class="icon website"></span></a></li><li><a href="https://universeodon.com/@scaine" title="External Link: https://universeodon.com/@scaine"><span class="icon mastodon"></span></a></li>
								</ul>
							</div>
							<div id="299941" class="comment-body">
								<div class="actual-comment-text" id="text_299941">
									<blockquote class="comment_quote"><cite>Quoting: <span class="username">tarmo888</span></cite>Never knew about this game, probably most people didn&#039;t. They probably knew it too, so they needed to expand the visibility with something edgy and started sending review keys to AI-haters for reaction. Seems like it worked, such an obvious trap.<br>
</blockquote>They might have expanded on visibility, but I&#039;m still not buying their shite.
								</div>
							<div class="likes"><span class="total_likes">2</span> Likes <span class="who-likes"><span class="emoji-summary"><span style="margin-right: 5px;">👍 (2)</span></span> <a href="#" data-ajax-modal data-page="likes" data-type="comment" data-id="299941">See more...</a></span></div>
							</div>
						</div>

						
						<a class="anchor" id="r299942"></a>
						<div class="comment group r299942 ">
							<div class="comment-meta group">
								<div class="comment-post">
									<span class="username"><img title="Fedora Silverblue" class="distro tooltip-top" alt="" src="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/templates/default/images/distros/Fedora%20Silverblue.svg"><a href="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/profiles/14269">mattaraxia</a></span>  <abbr title="2026-09-12T17:50:02+00:00" class="timeago">12 Sep 2026</abbr>  
								</div>
								<div class="comment-actions">
									<ul>
										<li><a class="tooltip-top" href="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/index.php?module=articles_full&amp;go=report_comment&amp;article_id=29744&amp;comment_id=299942" title="Report"><span class="icon flag">Flag</span></a></li>
										   
										<li><a href="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/2026/09/active-matter-developers-put-up-an-incredibly-distasteful-ai-notice-on-steam/?comment_id=299942" data-ajax-modal data-page="comment" data-id="299942" data-type="comment" class="post_link tooltip-top" title="Link to this comment"><span class="icon link">Link</span></a></li>
										
									</ul>
								</div>
							</div>
							<div class="comment-author hide-xsmall">
								<div class="avatar"><img class="avatar" src="https://www.gamingonlinux.com/uploads/avatars/generated/14269_generated_1783590472.png" alt="User Avatar"></div>
								<ul class="comment-badges">
									
									
									
								</ul>
								<ul class="comment-social">
									
								</ul>
							</div>
							<div id="299942" class="comment-body">
								<div class="actual-comment-text" id="text_299942">
									Not to defend them, but just to interpret this generously, the studio is . . . Hungarian right? Sometimes expressions like that hit very differently to people who speak English as a second language.<br>
<br>
It may be more unfortunate than offensive. I mean don&#039;t get me wrong, I&#039;m sure they were trying to make an edgy joke, but it probably hits real different among their peers than yours. I just try to treat these things like I would if I had say a coworker who spoke English as a second language and said something bizarre than assuming it&#039;s this either or like this article says. It&#039;s likely not so harsh as all that, but it certainly would be good if someone got them to change it.
								</div>
							<div class="likes likes_hidden "><span class="total_likes">0</span> Likes <span class="who-likes"></span></div>
							</div>
						</div>

					</div>
